course: dictionary
lesson: 2433
title: Dad and the clues around it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Dad is a word for your father. When you use it as a name, as in «Thanks, Dad!», it starts with a capital letter. The words around a word help you know what it means, and they often show what a person is like.
explain: «In Bradford, Tariq's dad, strict and religious and warm underneath, says no to a sleepover party, then drives Tariq there and picks him up at nine.» The clues are strict, warm underneath and drives him there. Dad says no, but he still helps, so he cares even when he is firm.
explain: Sometimes a dad says the opposite of what he means. «That's not the worst idea you've had» is a dry way of saying «good idea». Ask yourself what word would fit here, then try your meaning in the sentence. A smile and «let's do it» show what Dad really means.
fact: Dad means father.
fact: When Dad is used as a name, write it with a capital letter: «Thanks, Dad!»
fact: In the UK people often say «Mum and Dad»; in the USA they say «Mom and Dad».
fact: Dad can be part of other words, such as «stepdad», «granddad» and «daddy».
fact: The plural of dad is dads.
exercise: What does dad mean? | A grandmother | A cousin | *A father | A teacher who gives homework
exercise: In «Thanks, Dad!», why does Dad start with a capital letter? | Because it comes after a question mark | Because it is the longest word in the sentence | *Because it is used as a name | Because it is in the USA
exercise: Tariq's dad says no to the party, then drives him there. What does this show? | He never cares about Tariq | He wants Tariq to stay at home forever | *He is strict but he still helps | He is angry and shouts all day
test: What is the plural of dad? | dadds | dad's | *dads | dadies
test: «That's not the worst idea you've had» is a dry way of saying what? | a silly joke about sleeping over | *good idea | a rude word | the worst idea ever
exam: Which phrase is used in the UK for both parents? | Mom and Dad | Mam and Papa | Mum and Pa | *Mum and Dad
